@andyyang890 I see that we pull this number into docs on the Java row [here](https://www.cockroachlabs.com/docs/stable/third-party-database-tools#data-access-frameworks-e-g-orms) for CRDB 23.1+.

1. Should I make a change to the docs code so that this new supported version is only displayed for 23.2+? What we did [for 22.2](https://github.com/cockroachdb/docs/blob/main/src/current/_includes/v22.2/misc/tooling.md?plain=1#L48) is pull this Hibernate version from the `cockroach` `release-22.2` branch, so this value won't change based on what's on `master`. I assume it would make sense to similarly freeze the 23.1 number at 5.6.15, for now, pulling directly from the `release-23.1` branch. Would you agree?

2. The resulting text in the docs (from the current `cockroachdb:master`) is "5.6.15 (must be at least 5.4.19)". Only the first version number comes from `hibernate.go`. The parenthetical minimum version is hard-coded. I assume it's OK to leave that min version of 5.4.19 as-is; can you confirm?
